cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use telespec in research, please cite this software."
title: "telespec: Explainable spectral analysis for network telemetry"
abstract: >-
  telespec is an open-source Python toolkit for explainable spectral analysis
  and anomaly detection on irregularly sampled network telemetry. It applies a
  floating-mean generalized Lomb-Scargle periodogram directly to observed
  timestamps, calibrates peak significance with a permutation bootstrap, and
  reports anomalies as evidence-backed intervals with plain-language reasons.
